\title{rpkgfix: Diagnose and Fix Common R Package Problems}
\description{
\code{rpkgfix} is a dependency-light toolkit for R package authors. It is built
almost entirely on base R and splits its functions into two clear groups:
\itemize{
\item \strong{\verb{check_*()}} functions are \emph{read-only} diagnostics. They never modify
files and each returns an invisible list of \code{errors}, \code{warnings}, and
\code{notes} so they can be used programmatically (e.g. in CI).
\item \strong{Mutating helpers} (verb-first names such as \code{add_namespaces()},
\code{fix_buildignore()}, \code{bump_version()}, \code{clean_build()}) write to disk.
}
}
